 6. 💸 Trump&#x27;s reality check 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Eniola Odetunde/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump's proposal to send adult U.S. citizens $5,000 dividend checks if Republicans retain control of the House and the Senate would require congressional approval, House Speaker Mike Johnson (R-La.) said yesterday.

 Why it matters: Trump and his top officials claim they can send the checks without Congress — even with the prospect of them costing upward of $1.3 trillion, Axios' Ben Berkowitz writes. Asked on NBC's "Meet the Press" if he'd commit that the checks will be sent, Johnson said: "I commit that Congress will work through it and find consensus on that like they have to do everything else."

 Trump told reporters before departing Ireland yesterday that "the $5,000 checks are going forward" and that he had thought of this plan "a while ago." Share this story . 

 
 
